# Read by `op run --env-file` for `bin/release --npm-local` only (see bin/release
# and Hecks::Release::Runner). By default CI publishes @hecks/client with npm
# trusted publishing and this file is not used; --npm-local is the way to make
# the first publish, before a trusted publisher can be configured, and the
# fallback when CI is down.
#
# This holds an op:// REFERENCE, not a secret — safe to commit. `op run`
# resolves it at run time (unlocked by Touch ID) and injects it into
# `npm publish`'s one subprocess only. npm expands ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} in a
# throwaway user config, so the token is never written to disk.
#
# The token is the concealed field "publish token" on the "npmjs.com" item in
# the Hecks vault. Edit the vault, item or field here if yours differ.
#
# It must be a granular token with "Bypass two-factor authentication" enabled,
# scoped Read and write to the @hecks scope, and short-lived: the account's
# second factor is a passkey, so a token that requires a one-time code cannot
# publish (npm answers EOTP). The publish also passes --auth-type=web, so if npm
# does ask for a passkey approval it prints a link and waits; that is the
# interactive fallback.
NODE_AUTH_TOKEN="op://Hecks/npmjs.com/publish token"
